<title>CANADA: Alberta Wheat Pool downgrades crop outlook.</title>
<headline>Alberta Wheat Pool downgrades crop outlook.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alberta Wheat Pool on Friday downgraded its crop outlook despite a slight improvement in soil moisture conditions.</p>
<p>AWP's crop condition index of 100 represents optimal growing conditions while 50 represents average crop output.</p>
<p>CROPS			 CONDITIONS INDEX</p>
<p>				This Wk  June 27  June 20  July 4/96</p>
<p>Hard Red Spring Wheat    74	 78	 80	 78</p>
<p>Can Prairie Spring Wheat 75	 76	 80	 80</p>
<p>Soft White Spring Wheat  63	 69	 61	 63</p>
<p>Winter Wheat		 64	 66	 62	 64</p>
<p>Durum Wheat		  64	 66	 67	 73</p>
<p>Oats			   72	 73	 79	 80</p>
<p>Barley			 73	 76	 80	 80</p>
<p>Flax			   54	 56	 71	 55</p>
<p>Canola			 71	 76	 77	 78</p>
<p>Fall Rye		     67	 71	 68	 73</p>
<p>AVERAGE CROP CONDITION:  73	 76	 79	 78</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
